why: the first branch of `claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi` returns false where the standard API is absent, and the fact is why: opening a scheme session on a ledger with only a prefixed interface spends a posting budget on a scheme the service's current pipeline never uses; run 10 routed it to the human as fitting nowhere, and the branch that performs the act is in this function
labelled: 2026-09-24
--- code
export async function claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi(scheme: PostingScheme, formatName: string): Promise<boolean> {
  if (typeof ledgerApi.requestSchemeAccess !== 'function') {
    return false;
  }

  for (const schemeId of listSchemeIds(scheme)) {
    if ((await askScheme({ schemeId, formatName })) === LedgerClaim.Accepted) {
      return true;
    }
  }

  return false;
}
--- facts
`claimsSchemeThroughStandardApi` asks each scheme id with no settlement mode.

# claimed at this site by an earlier run:
A ledger with only a prefixed interface answers no, because opening a scheme session there would spend a full posting budget on a scheme the service's current pipeline does not use.
